==Trivia==
*This is the first season where 14 houseguests voted in the first eviction. The prior seasons that featured 17 houseguests did not feature this for a variety of reasons:
**In ''[[Big Brother 17 (US)]]'', the [[Julia Nolan|17th houseguest]] did not officially join the game [[Project DNA|until Week 6]], so Week 1 featured the standard 16 houseguests with 13 casting votes.
**In ''[[Big Brother 19 (US)]]'', the first eviction was a [[Premiere Night Eviction]] which featured 3 nominees, and the [[Paul Abrahamian|17th houseguest]] was only allowed to vote in the event of tie as part of the [[Big Brother Swap]] twist, leaving only 13 voting houseguests.
**In ''[[Big Brother 25 (US)]]'', the [[Cirie Fields|17th houseguest]] had already joined the game and was allowed to vote, so the first eviction was ''intended'' to have 14 voting houseguests. However, [[Luke Valentine|another player]] was [[Ejection|expelled]] from the game during the week, and production chose to continue on with the eviction as scheduled, leaving 16 houseguests and 13 casting votes as normal.
*This is the first season where every male houseguest was nominated for eviction at least once by Week 5.
**This feat was almost accomplished during ''[[Big Brother 13 (US)]]'', but was not truly achieved due to [[Dick Donato]] having walked from the game in Week 1.
*This is the first season to feature an 8-3 gender split at the Final 11, in the favor of the women.
*This is the first season since ''[[Big Brother 4 (US)]]'' to have a second consecutive woman winner after the prior season.

